previous 5 years. patients with intraepithelial squamos cell carcinoma of the skin (bowen’s
disease) treated with topical 5fu and subjects with basal cell skin cancer are allowed to enter
the trial"""^^xsd:string .

    <https://w3id.org/CMEO/leader/number_of_participants> a cmeo:number_of_participants ;
        rdfs:label "number of participants"^^xsd:string ;
        ro:is_part_of <https://w3id.org/CMEO/leader/randomized_controlled_trial/protocol> ;
        cmeo:has_value "9341"^^xsd:string .

    <https://w3id.org/CMEO/leader/objective_specification> a obi:objective_specification ;
        cmeo:has_value "patients with type 2 diabetes and high cardiovascular risk to receive liraglutide or placebo. the primary composite outcome in the time-to-event analysis was the first occurrence of death from cardiovascular causes, nonfatal myocardial infarction, or nonfatal stroke. the primary hypothesis was that liraglutide would be noninferior to placebo"^^xsd:string .

    <https://w3id.org/CMEO/leader/outcome_specification> a cmeo:outcome_specification ;
        rdfs:label "outcome specification"^^xsd:string ;
        ro:has_part <https://w3id.org/CMEO/leader/primary_outcome_specification>,
            <https://w3id.org/CMEO/leader/secondary_outcome_specification> .

    <https://w3id.org/CMEO/leader/primary_outcome_specification> a cmeo:primary_outcome_specification ;
        rdfs:label "primary outcome specification"^^xsd:string ;
        cmeo:has_value """to assess the effect of treatment with liraglutide compared to placebo for at least 3.5 year and up
to 5 years on the incidence of cardiovascular events, as defined by the below primary and
secondary endpoints, in adults with type 2 diabetes that are at high risk for cardiovascular events. the primary objective will be addressed using the following primary endpoint:
time from randomisation to first occurrence of cardiovascular death, non-fatal myocardial
infarction, or non-fatal stroke (a composite cardiovascular outcome)  """^^xsd:string .

    <https://w3id.org/CMEO/leader/secondary_outcome_specification> a cmeo:secondary_outcome_specification ;
        rdfs:label "secondary outcome specification"^^xsd:string ;
        cmeo:has_value """to assess the efficacy and safety with regard to clinically important events or other surrogate
parameters of treatment with liraglutide compared to placebo in adults with type 2 diabetes that
are at high risk for cardiovascular events. the following secondary endpoints will be used as supportive endpoints for the primary objective:
time from randomisation to first occurrence of an expanded composite cardiovascular
outcome, defined as either cardiovascular death, non-fatal myocardial infarction, non-fatal
stroke, revascularisation, unstable angina or hospitalisation for chronic heart failure; time from randomisation to all cause death; time from randomisation to each individual component of the expanded composite
cardiovascular outcome  """^^xsd:string .

